The diagram is a coordinate grid representing Earth's surface.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=14mm,y=12mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw[xstep=14mm,ystep=12mm,color={rgb,255:red,204;green,204;blue,204}] (-2,-1) grid (2,1);
\draw[thick] (-2,0)--(2,0);
\draw[thick] (0,-1)--(0,1);
\node[left] at (-2,1) {$15^\circ\mathrm{N}$};
\node[left] at (-2,0) {$0^\circ$};
\node[left] at (-2,-1) {$15^\circ\mathrm{S}$};
\node[below] at (-2,-1) {$90^\circ\mathrm{W}$};
\node[below] at (-1,-1) {$45^\circ\mathrm{W}$};
\node[below] at (0,-1) {$0^\circ$};
\node[below] at (1,-1) {$45^\circ\mathrm{E}$};
\node[below] at (2,-1) {$90^\circ\mathrm{E}$};
\fill[black] (1,1) circle (1.8pt);
\node[above right] at (1,1) {$A$};
\fill[black] (-1,-1) circle (1.8pt);
\node[above right] at (-1,-1) {$B$};
\fill[black] (2,0) circle (1.8pt);
\node[above right] at (2,0) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a. Write the coordinates of point $A$.

b. Name the point at $(15^\circ\mathrm{S},45^\circ\mathrm{W})$.
